 {:name "normalize-integer-complex-casts-before-projections"
  :level :lemma-location
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Prove a complex equality by real and imaginary parts when the expression contains integers cast directly into ℂ, especially floor terms."
   :symptom
   "After `Complex.ext` and expansion with `Complex.add_re`, `Complex.mul_re`, `Complex.add_im`, and `Complex.mul_im`, goals retain terms such as `(↑⌊x⌋ : ℂ).re` and `(↑⌊x⌋ : ℂ).im`; `Complex.ofReal_re` and `Complex.ofReal_im` do not match those direct integer casts."
   :lemma "`Complex.ofReal_intCast`"
   :before
   "`simp only [Complex.ofReal_re, Complex.ofReal_im, ...]` leaves integer-cast projections opaque, so `linarith`, `ring`, `omega`, and `push_cast` cannot see the real floor identities."
   :after
   "Include `← Complex.ofReal_intCast` before `Complex.ofReal_re` and `Complex.ofReal_im` in the simplification set. The integer-to-complex cast is first normalized to an integer-to-real cast followed by `Complex.ofReal`; the projection lemmas then reduce it to a real integer cast."
   :rewrite-rule
   "Normalize the source cast into the constructor expected by a projection lemma before trying to simplify the projection."
   :successful-shape
   ["Apply `Complex.ext`."
    "Expand addition, multiplication, and I projections."
    "Rewrite with `← Complex.ofReal_intCast`."
    "Simplify `Complex.ofReal_re`/`Complex.ofReal_im`."
    "Finish with the real identities `Int.fract_add_floor` and `linarith`."]
   :scope
   "Direct `ℤ → ℂ` casts under `.re` or `.im`. The broader tactic applies whenever a simplification lemma is stated for an intermediate constructor rather than the original coercion path."}
